Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to preserve per-key order under contention while enabling global throughput and dynamic resource scaling. It also probes backpressure handling, fairness across many topics, and safe shutdowns.

Key Concepts
- Bounded queues and backpressure
- Per-topic FIFO ordering
- Dynamic worker pool with runtime reconfiguration
- Fair scheduling across topics and avoidance of starvation
- Graceful shutdown that drains in-flight tasks per topic

